/*--------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  LABBAN 2017 -- NaCl + MgCl2, heldout rows

  LbL-C hollow-fibre NF membrane, NaCl + MgCl2 mixture, observed ion rejections at 3 bar -- the HELD-OUT (3 bar) rows.
  REJECTIONS and FLUX: Table 7 (accepted manuscript p. 21, journal p. 26), read on the page image,
  every value a TABLE value (rejection in % there, a fraction here; flux in LMH there, m/s here:
  1 LMH = 1/3.6e6 m/s).  The ion rows are the OBSERVED rejections 1 - c_p/c_b of each ion.
  FEED: Table 6, row NaCl + MgCl2: Na 398.6, Mg 254.2, Cl 1351 (mg/kg).  Salts from the measured cations and sulfate (the article
  measured them by ICP-OES; chloride follows by electroneutrality), molar masses of the catalogue
  species records, density 1 kg/L assumed.  Written as salts because DSPM-DE decomposes them.
  The `fit` / `heldout` split of the three pressures is this case's: 2 and 4 bar fit, 3 bar held out.
\*--------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

property     membrane.rejection;
membrane     LbLC;

provenance
{
    source       measured;
    reviewStatus checked;
    citation     "O. Labban, C. Liu, T. H. Chong, J. H. Lienhard V, Fundamentals of low-pressure nanofiltration: Membrane characterization, modeling, and understanding the multi-ionic interactions in water softening, J. Membr. Sci. 521 (2017) 18-32, doi:10.1016/j.memsci.2016.08.062, Table 7 and Table 6";
    identity     "one series of the study cited above (accepted manuscript read page by page as images and the journal version for the tables); no doi identity of its own";
    licence      "facts: numbers transcribed from a published article (Elsevier copyright); the article and its figures are not in the tree";
}

T            298.15 K;     // ASSUMED: the article states no temperature (see the case README)
feed         { NaCl 17.3380 mol/m3; MgCl2 10.4588 mol/m3; }

columns
(
    { name Jv;  unit m/s; }
    { name R_Na;  unit -; }
    { name R_Mg;  unit -; }
    { name R_Cl;  unit -; }
);

data
(
    5.333333e-06  -0.0170  0.9920  0.4900
);
